WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.857
This analytics view exposes subject ID, age band, city, and active status.

00:00:04.857 --> 00:00:07.992
It omits name, email, and date of birth.

00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:10.212
That creates a narrower analytical interface.

00:00:10.212 --> 00:00:16.637
Run it and compare the result with the source patient table.

00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:22.757
The design reduces unnecessary fields, but access to objects must still be configured separately.

00:00:22.757 --> 00:00:27.937
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:27.937 --> 00:00:34.237
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:34.237 --> 00:00:40.273
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
